{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,16]],"date-time":"2026-09-16T19:18:35Z","timestamp":1789586315335,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":19,"publisher":"American Geophysical Union (AGU)","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,16]],"date-time":"2009-01-16T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1232064000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":15,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Geophysical Research Letters"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>\n                    Nearly all energy used for human purposes is dissipated as heat within Earth's land\u2013atmosphere system. Thermal energy released from non\u2010renewable sources is therefore a climate forcing term. Averaged globally, this forcing is only +0.028 W m\n                    <jats:sup>\u22122<\/jats:sup>\n                    , but over the continental United States and western Europe, it is +0.39 and +0.68 W m\n                    <jats:sup>\u22122<\/jats:sup>\n                    , respectively. Here, present and future global inventories of anthropogenic heat flux (AHF) are developed, and parameterizations derived for seasonal and diurnal flux cycles. Equilibrium climate experiments show statistically\u2010significant continental\u2010scale surface warming (0.4\u20130.9\u00b0C) produced by one 2100 AHF scenario, but not by current or 2040 estimates. However, significant increases in annual\u2010mean temperature and planetary boundary layer (PBL) height occur over gridcells where present\u2010day AHF exceeds 3.0 W m\n                    <jats:sup>\u22122<\/jats:sup>\n                    . PBL expansion leads to a slight, but significant increase in atmospheric residence time of aerosols emitted from large\u2010AHF regions. Hence, AHF may influence regional climate projections and contemporary chemistry\u2010climate studies.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1029\/2008gl036465","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,15]],"date-time":"2009-01-15T16:41:59Z","timestamp":1232037719000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":240,"title":["Integrating anthropogenic heat flux with global climate models"],"prefix":"10.1029","volume":"36","author":[{"given":"Mark G.","family":"Flanner","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Advanced Study Program National Center for Atmospheric Research  Boulder Colorado USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"13","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,16]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s10546-004-4834-5"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2003JD003697"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2008EO280001"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1175\/JCLI3761.1"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.atmosenv.2004.03.032"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2004JD005192"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.atmosenv.2004.09.031"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/91WR00557"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S1352-2310(99)00132-6"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0957-1272(91)90050-O"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.atmosenv.2005.11.061"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1023\/A:1002463829265"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1177\/030913338801200401"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1175\/2007JAMC1598.1"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1175\/2007JAMC1597.1"},{